WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.920
"The Expendables" movies were once massively&nbsp;
popular — so why are audiences treating the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:11.520
fourth movie like it's, well, expendable? Here's&nbsp;
why "The Expendables 4" was a box office dud.
 &nbsp;

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.320
Let's address the biggest elephant in a&nbsp;
room full of them: "The Expendables 4"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:20.040
performed badly because of its extremely poor&nbsp;
reception among critics. The film scored a bad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.280
Rotten Tomatoes record, hitting an initial&nbsp;
rating of just 15% on the Tomatometer after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:29.960
84 reviews. That number places it among&nbsp;
some of the worst-rated films of 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.600
such as "Fool's Paradise" and&nbsp;
"Winnie the Pooh: Blood and Honey."

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.640
Many critics have singled out "The Expendables&nbsp;
4" for having a barebones plot, poor performances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:45.240
from the cast, and lackluster action sequences&nbsp;
cluttered with low-quality CGI. In its review,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.280
Looper's sister site /Film gave&nbsp;
the movie a score of 3/10, writing,

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:55.560
"The characters are inhuman, the premise is&nbsp;
absurd, and the plot is idiotic. This is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:01.960
Saturday Morning cartoon with booze, f-bombs,&nbsp;
and a mild libido. It's staggeringly stupid."

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.680
According to Deadline, "The Expendables 4"&nbsp;
had a fairly small advertising budget of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:11.040
just $20 million in the run-up to its debut. As&nbsp;
such, it's likely that the film completely flew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.440
under the radar for many casual consumers who&nbsp;
otherwise might have been interested in seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:19.360
it. Deadline further suggested that the lack&nbsp;
of advertising surrounding "The Expendables&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.880
4" was actually a conscious effort on the&nbsp;
part of the film's distributor Lionsgate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:27.240
as the company surmised that the movie&nbsp;
was not going to be received well.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.440
To further complicate matters, the road to the&nbsp;
premiere of "The Expendables 4" took place amid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:37.160
the 2023 SAG-AFTRA strike and the WGA strike.&nbsp;
So a lot of the film's cast couldn't promote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.640
their projects during the strikes, as doing so&nbsp;
would constitute crossing the picket line. Thus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:46.280
"The Expendable 4" saw its release in&nbsp;
September with little to no fanfare.
 &nbsp;

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:49.760
If there was ever something that could be&nbsp;
remotely considered a zeitgeist surrounding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.200
"The Expendables," it happened in the early&nbsp;
2010s. Back when these movies first released,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.360
they built on each previous entry in quick&nbsp;
succession with more action-packed plots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:01.480
and eye-popping cast additions.&nbsp;
That's why the nine-year wait for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:04.960
"The Expendables 4" has made it&nbsp;
feel like it's late to the party.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.720
The landscape of Hollywood looks quite different&nbsp;
compared to the last time "The Expendables"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:12.760
reared its head. Streaming has changed the&nbsp;
way people watch movies, and companies need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:17.240
to work harder than ever to provide convincing&nbsp;
reasons for audiences to head to the theater.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.640
Rival franchises like "Fast and Furious" and&nbsp;
"Mission: Impossible" have grown even bigger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:26.240
filling the vacuum left by movies like the early&nbsp;
"Expendables" films. Audience tastes have shifted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:30.400
too. With superhero movie fatigue and&nbsp;
sequel/reboot exhaustion growing ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:35.200
more pertinent, the tolerance for a clunky&nbsp;
action movie revival is at an all-time low.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.280
To say that "The Expendables" never&nbsp;
had a chance at seeing success after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:42.000
such a long stint away from theater&nbsp;
screens isn't quite right. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.200
if the franchise really wanted to stand out in&nbsp;
the modern day, it needed to grow past what it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.440
once was and deliver something compelling.&nbsp;
Instead, "The Expendables 4" has slid in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:56.040
the opposite direction, and failed to match the&nbsp;
spectacle and fun factor of the earlier films.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.280
"Hey, why don't we have dinner?"

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.720
"Sure, when?"

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.080
"In a thousand years."

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:01.520
"Too soon."

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:05.400
If there's one thing big blockbuster action&nbsp;
movies are known for, it's their uncanny knack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.760
for landing casts filled with recognizable&nbsp;
talent. "The Expendables 4" isn't a complete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:14.920
slouch on this front, as it unites returning&nbsp;
franchise actors like Sylvester Stallone, Jason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:20.400
Statham and Dolph Lundgren with new additions&nbsp;
like 50 Cent and Megan Fox. However, it's tough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:25.600
to deny that its cast list pales in comparison&nbsp;
to the star-studded line-ups of previous entries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:30.880
which included massive names like Harrison&nbsp;
Ford, Arnold Schwarzenegger and Chuck Norris.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:32.480
"Rumor has it you were dead?"

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.600
"Yeah, I heard that, too.&nbsp;
So how's life treating you?"

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:39.200
There's nothing inherently wrong with having&nbsp;
a movie cast that isn't completely stuffed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.160
with huge A-list celebrities. However, "The&nbsp;
Expendables" has a legacy of doing just that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.600
and the star power behind this fourth entry in&nbsp;
the series feels weak compared to what has come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:52.960
before. With few actors to draw general&nbsp;
audiences in on name recognition alone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.200
the film isn't as popular as it could have been.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.440
Some would-be viewers may have also been put off&nbsp;
by a certain shift in dynamic among returning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:03.520
stars for "The Expendables 4." While Stallone's&nbsp;
character, Barney Ross, has historically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.640
been the face of the franchise, pre-release&nbsp;
information on the movie made it apparent that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:12.920
he was passing the starring role over to Jason&nbsp;
Statham's Lee Christmas for this latest entry.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.040
"Why are you here?"

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.280
"I got this situation where I need your help."

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:18.440
"I need better friends."

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:22.160
That's a change that may have rubbed&nbsp;
at least a few fans the wrong way.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:26.480
There are a lot of problems with "The Expendables&nbsp;
4" that contributed to its box office failure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:29.600
but solely placing the blame on the&nbsp;
movie itself would unfairly ignore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:33.680
the difficult path that "The Expendables&nbsp;
3" set up for it nearly a decade ago.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:37.760
For those less familiar with the history of the&nbsp;
franchise, "The Expendables 4" is not the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:42.520
critical stinker in the saga. At the time of&nbsp;
its release in 2014, "The Expendables 3" was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:46.840
similarly panned by critics for failing to&nbsp;
live up to the expectations set by the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:51.240
two movies. It stands to reason that some&nbsp;
fans who felt burned by "The Expendables 3"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:55.480
may have written off "The Expendables 4" just&nbsp;
by virtue of the quality of its predecessor.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:59.600
One also has to account for the fact that being&nbsp;
the fourth movie in a franchise can be a bit of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.840
tough sell. Some potential viewers might be under&nbsp;
the impression that watching previous entries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:08.400
in the series is required in order to understand&nbsp;
what's happening in the newest film. Then, there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:12.880
the simple fact that sequels are risky commercial&nbsp;
territory for just about any franchise. Some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:17.440
sequels fare better than the original in terms of&nbsp;
box office performance, but others can't manage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:21.400
the same level of retention. "The Expendables&nbsp;
3" already had a lower box office gross than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:25.699
"The Expendables 2." So "The Expendables&nbsp;
4" is just following that downward trend.

